The README still said 'No patch content is included in this Phase-1 skeleton' and 'Phase 1 is
a repository skeleton and provenance layer only'. Both were false once the 38-patch series
landed, and a stranger reading them would have concluded the fork was empty.

Adds, per charter ask #1:
- what this fork adds to upstream, per feature, each with its toggle, default and an HONEST
  status - measured gain, measured loss, or UNMEASURED where we have no number;
- honest negative results, including the ones that cost us: the thecodacus patches measuring
  inert on unified memory, DSpark at 0.54x, TurboQuant KV losing to plain q4_0, and a NaN
  this fork caused itself and fixed;
- how a user reproduces our numbers, including the --no-host requirement, without which a
  CPU_REPACK A/B silently tests nothing - the exact trap that produced two false passes here;
- how to maintain and bump the fork with tools/arifi-sync.

Credits were already complete and correct and are left as they stand: thecodacus with his
repo, the three commit links and the video; PrismML, PowerInfer, ROCmFPX, TurboQuant.

